{"agent":"impl-sw-conformance","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A stub agent replaying tool events plus a revocation file shows claim/heartbeat/gate/lease-stop through the Lane contract's canonical tool events.","falsifier":"An obeying stub stays running after revocation, or an ignoring stub is graded passed.","item":"SW-conformance","mechanism":"process-headless maps JSON lines to canonical tool events (stream_map), status() reports running vs exited, so revocation-then-exit is observable.","probe":"uv run pytest tests/test_lane_conformance.py -q (x3)","probe_output":"19 passed in 3.47s (three runs); an early draft refuted a naive 'no tool call after revoke' rule (buffered pre-revoke events counted as after) and a self-exiting lane being graded as obeying; both fixed and tested","question":"Can lane conformance levels be proven with a stub agent on the process-headless driver, without real keys?","sources":["docs/ddflow/research/swarm-orchestration.md","docs/ddflow/lane-driver.md"],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e1b63dea188894fff9d3778b1","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":115415,"schema":1,"subject":"R53fed9e7dc","ts":"2026-10-30T18:39:16.992365Z"}
